      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-44833",
      ":question/problem": "A bouquet of flowers consists of $3$ roses, $4$ tulips and $5$ violets. The cost of one rose is $R$ dollars, the cost of one tulip is $T$ dollars and the cost of one violet is $V$ dollars. Max is purchasing some bouquets for a wedding, and his total bill comes to $8(3R + 4T + 5V)$ dollars.\n\nWhat does the factor $8$ mean in this context?"
